WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.167
Thank you very much, Mr.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.002
President.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.571
No, it was

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.741
it was one year ago this week,

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.042
and we spoke on the telephone.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.410
Mr. President.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.079
It was very late in night in Washington.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.016
Early in the morning here in Kiev.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.117
Russian planes were in

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:17.617
the air

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.785
and tanks were rolling

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.720
across your border.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.789
You told me

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.125
that you could hear the explosions

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.459
in the background.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.294
I'll never forget that

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.532
and the world was about to change.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.634
I remember it vividly

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.537
because I asked to I asked you next.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:41.141
I asked you what is there, Mr.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.108
President,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.577
what can I do for you?

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.913
How can I be of help?

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.082
And I know they remember what you said

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.418
to me, what you said, and I quote,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.387
gather the leaders of the world,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.956
ask them

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.225
to support Ukraine.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.162
Gather the leaders of the world

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.731
and ask them to support Ukraine.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.334
And you said you didn't know

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.372
when we would be able to speak again

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.340
that dark night

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.209
one year ago,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.511
the world was literally at the time

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.881
bracing for the fall in Kyiv.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.384
Seems like a lot longer ago than a year.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.087
But think back to that year,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.091
perhaps even the end of Ukraine.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.326
You know,

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.296
one year later, Kyiv stands

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.833
and Ukraine stands.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.001
Democracy stands

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.504
The Americans stand with you

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.073
and the world stands with you.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.642
Kyiv has captured a part of my heart,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.077
I must say,

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.912
I've come here six times

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.648
as vice president, once as president,

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.786
and in 2009 as vice president.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.921
And I first came here,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.157
then back in 20, 14.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.092
I came three times in the aftermath of

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.327
the revolution of dignity.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.062
And I

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.097
again came in 2015

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.434
to address the Rada

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.070
about the work of building

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.672
a strong democracy

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.975
and I came in 2017

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.511
just before I left office

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.379
as Vice President

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.681
I knew I'd be back,

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.017
but I wanted to be sure,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.920
even though the election were over,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.823
Barack and I were out of office.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.592
I decided to make one more trip

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.495
before the next president was sworn in

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.863
to Kyiv.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.834
So President Zelensky you deeply honor me

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.905
here in key with you today

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.141
to meet with your military,

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.042
your intelligence,

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.678
folks, your diplomatic teams,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.681
community leaders who have stepped up

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.950
and helped their country

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.754
in their hour of need is astounding.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.988
Who stood up?

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.423
Everybody.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.625
Everybody.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.093
Women,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.362
young children.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.897
Try to do some of this, trying to

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:18.565
do something

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.135
pulling people out of apartments

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.203
have been shelled.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.671
And literally,

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.473
that I think, is a war crimes.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.943
It's astounding

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.178
in the whole world.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.747
The whole world sees it

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.250
and looks at it.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.553
This is the largest land war in Europe

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.723
in three quarters of a century.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.959
And you're succeeding

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.661
against all and every expectation

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.430
except your own.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.965
We have every confidence

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:52.398
that you're going

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.501
to continue to prevail and

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.603
you know,

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.939
from the moment I

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:00.773
first received

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.543
an intelligence report in the fall,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.311
about a year ago,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.514
we were focused on determining

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:13.353
how do we rally the rest of the world.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.488
How do I help you with the promise

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.991
you asked me to make, to rally the world?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.660
Well,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.763
how do you succeed?

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.833
How do you get a world to respond?

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.103
To a prosperous

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.338
economy, confident democracy,

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:37.310
a secure and independent state?

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.512
When united Americans

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.581
of all political backgrounds decided

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:45.151
they would step up

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.420
American people, no matters.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.124
Unchecked aggression

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.593
is a threat to all of us.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.261
We build a coalition of nations

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:58.231
from the Atlantic to the Pacific

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.133
NATO's

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.069
to the land, the Atlantic,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.437
Japan and the Pacific.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:07.507
I mean, across the across the world.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:10.176
The number of nations that have over 50

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.981
help Ukraine defend itself.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.349
Unprecedented military,

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.252
economic and humanitarian support.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.154
We united the leading economies

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.723
of the world to impose unprecedented cost

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.492
that are squeezing Russia's

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.795
economic lifelines.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.229
Together,

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.598
we've committed nearly 700 tanks

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.735
and thousands of armored vehicles,

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.971
1000 artillery systems,

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.541
more than 2 million rounds

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.943
of artillery ammunition,

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.311
more than 50 advanced

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.347
launch rocket systems

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.849
and AI ship and air defense systems.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.119
All defend you to defend Ukraine.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.821
And that doesn't count

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:56.189
the other half a billion dollars.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.190
We're going to be

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.891
we're announcing with you today

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.093
and tomorrow.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.329
That's going to be coming your way.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:03.663
And that's

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:06.733
just the United States in this piece.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.668
And just today,

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.770
that announcement includes

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.838
artillery ammunition

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:14.006
for high marks and Howitzers,

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.342
more javelins and the armor systems,

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.277
air surveillance radars to help protect

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.147
Ukrainian people from aerial bombardment.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:23.983
Later this week,

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.719
we will announce additional sanctions

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.721
against elites and companies

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.423
that are trying to evade sanctions

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.526
and backfill Russia's war machine.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.561
And thanks to bipartisan support

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.996
in Congress

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.332
this week, we're delivering billions

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.901
in direct budgetary support,

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.570
billions in direct budgetary support,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.371
which the government

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.774
can put to use immediately

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.275
to help provide for basic

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.610
services of citizens.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.946
The cost that Ukraine has had

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.282
to bear has been extraordinarily high,

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.986
and the sacrifices

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:01.921
have been far too great.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:02.789
They've been met with them

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:05.358
and far too great.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.627
We mourn alongside the families of those

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:09.028
who've been lost to the brutal

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:11.164
and unjust war.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.566
We know that there will be very difficult

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.868
days and weeks and years ahead.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.004
But Russia's aim

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:20.072
was to wipe Ukraine off the map

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.643
Putin's war conquest

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.578
is failing

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:28.080
Russia's military has lost

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.349
half its territory once occupied

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.386
young town, and Russians

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.822
are fleeing by the tens of thousands

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:39.725
not wanting to come back to Russia.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:40.293
Not from

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.528
not just fleeing from the military,

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.631
fleeing from Russia itself.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:47.967
Because they see

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.670
no future in their country.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.472
Russia's economy

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:55.141
is now a backwater,

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:56.576
isolated, is struggling

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:01.481
Putin thought Ukraine was weak

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:04.116
and the West was divided.

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:05.485
As you know, Mr.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:05.852
President,

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:06.819
I said to you in the beginning,

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.955
he's counting on us

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:11.123
not sticking together.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:13.059
He was counting on an inability

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:16.128
to keep NATO's united

00:08:16.596 --> 00:08:17.530
Is counting on us

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.565
not to be able to bring in others

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:23.503
on the side of Ukraine.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:26.772
He thought he could outlast us.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.140
I don't think he's thinking that

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.275
right now.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.244
God knows what he's thinking.

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:33.579
I don't think he's thinking that

00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:37.149
he's just been plain wrong.

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:39.385
Plain wrong.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.588
And one year later,

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:46.125
the evidence is right here in this room.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:48.561
We stand here together.

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:49.328
Mr.

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:50.296
President,

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.999
I'm delighted to be able

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:56.068
to repay your visit to our country

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.570
in Washington.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.204
Not long ago,

00:08:58.204 --> 00:08:58.871
you told us,

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:00.506
you told the Congress,

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:03.209
quote, We have no fear

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.011
nor should anyone in the world have it.

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:05.811
And of, quote,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.782
you and all Ukrainians.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.419
Mr.
President, remind the world

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.621
every single day

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:19.392
what the meaning of the word courage is.

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:21.961
From all sectors, your economy,

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:24.830
all walks of life.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.866
It's astounding.

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:28.768
Astounding

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:31.437
Remind us of freedom

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:33.573
is priceless.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.175
It's worth fighting for,

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:38.611
for as long as it takes.

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.112
And that's how long we're going to be

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.614
with you, Mr. President.

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:44.016
For as long as it takes.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.551
We'll do it. Thank you.

